{"parentUuid":"2d1dc06a-2d66-4e8a-b282-a2890f98cc54","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeCJRt1gF3FzQ625969eA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1470,"cache_read_input_tokens":30047,"output_tokens":970,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1470,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":970,"cache_read_input_tokens":30047,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1470,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1470},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCJRr3N55hCrgQyUu59a","type":"assistant","uuid":"c55c9e7f-95e9-4ad7-afff-b3cf7ab26600","timestamp":"2026-08-19T14:56:16.013Z","session_id":"c7c36682-05b9-475d-a948-e4b68ed9bf8a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/tunc","sessionId":"c7c36682-05b9-475d-a948-e4b68ed9bf8a","version":"2.1.211","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"compiled-napping-storm"}
{"parentUuid":"c55c9e7f-95e9-4ad7-afff-b3cf7ab26600","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeCJRt1gF3FzQ625969eA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Short answer: yes, but not entirely on the GPU — a 27B-class model won't fit in your 12GB of VRAM, so it'll run partially on CPU at modest speed.\n\nYour specs: RTX 3080 Ti (12GB VRAM, ~1.4GB currently used by Hyprland/Steam/etc.), 32GB RAM, i7-12700K, plenty of disk.\n\nOne note: there's no \"Qwen 3.8 27B\" — Qwen3's lineup is 0.6/1.7/4/8/14/32B dense plus a 30B-A3B MoE (the 27B you may be thinking of is Google's Gemma 3 27B). Here's how the candidates land on your hardware:\n\n- **27B–32B dense (Gemma 3 27B, Qwen3 32B)**: at 4-bit quantization that's ~16–20GB of weights, so roughly half offloads to system RAM. It runs fine with Ollama or llama.cpp, but expect maybe ~5–10 tokens/sec. Usable for chat, sluggish for long generations.\n- **Qwen3 30B-A3B (MoE)** — probably what you actually want: it's 30B parameters but only ~3B active per token, so even with weights split between VRAM and RAM it's fast (often 20+ tokens/sec). Best quality-per-speed fit for your machine.\n- **Qwen3 14B**: fits fully in 12GB VRAM at 4-bit and flies (30–60+ tokens/sec) if you'd rather stay all-GPU.\n\nIf you want to try it, `ollama` is the easiest route on Arch: `sudo pacman -S ollama-cuda`, then `ollama run qwen3:30b-a3b` (or `qwen3:14b` / `gemma3:27b`). Happy to set it up for you."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1470,"cache_read_input_tokens":30047,"output_tokens":970,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1470,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":970,"cache_read_input_tokens":30047,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1470,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1470},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCJRr3N55hCrgQyUu59a","type":"assistant","uuid":"be2c6861-4a5d-47f9-8f31-b1e50f8b808c","timestamp":"2026-08-19T14:56:16.030Z","session_id":"c7c36682-05b9-475d-a948-e4b68ed9bf8a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/tunc","sessionId":"c7c36682-05b9-475d-a948-e4b68ed9bf8a","version":"2.1.211","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"compiled-napping-storm"}
